WEBVTT

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:17.570
I'm okay.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:37.360
Are you going home?

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:09.650
- Do you have one maybe with Elsie on it?

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:10.550
- No Elsie.

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:13.750
- No Elsie's, well, we'll take a clown for our young lady.

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:19.400
Take our clown day.

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:10.250
- Why didn't you wait for her?

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:12.830
- She went home with someone else.

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:15.840
We wanted to wait for her.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:17.220
We did Mrs. Costa.

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:48.910
- Again in this case, as in the others,

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:52.090
the only clue is the missing shoes.

00:07:52.090 --> 00:07:56.110
I promise you your police force will find this murderer.

00:07:56.110 --> 00:07:58.200
To prevent other such crimes,

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.000
your police department has prepared five

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:08.090
don'ts. Don't let your children accept rides from strangers. Sometimes these are

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:14.010
one-way rides leading to death. The amiable stranger may be a killer. Don't

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:19.540
let your children accept presents from strangers. A bag of popcorn or a candy

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:25.630
bar is not worth your child's life. Don't send children on after-dark errands. The

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:30.000
night works in behalf of the killer who preys on our young. If you

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:36.370
must have something from a store after sundown get it yourself. Don't let your child play unattended

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:42.500
in wooded places or empty lots. Though your eyes aren't on him, someone else's may be watching.

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:50.690
Don't let your children become friendly with Pop, that nice old character in your neighborhood. Most

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:56.300
of these men are harmless, but there are exceptions. It's up to you to make sure your

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:59.060
child isn't the victim of one of these exceptions.

00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:04.080
And now, for one all-important do.

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:08.390
If you notice any suspicious characters lurking around schools and playgrounds,

00:09:08.390 --> 00:09:10.050
do call at once.

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:14.050
Your police department, Central 5000.

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:21.010
The life you save may be your child's life.

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:23.290
You have just heard Police Chief Regan making a...

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:26.930
What does he mean the kids were neither violated nor outraged?

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:29.600
What's the difference? He killed them, didn't he?

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:02.270
What's the matter, you trying to get your name in the paper?

00:10:02.270 --> 00:10:04.700
There's a crosswalk, 15th year up the street.

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:05.700
Ordinance 236, jaywalking.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:06.700
What's your name?

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:07.700
What are you picking on me for?

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:09.700
A million people every day jaywalking.

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:11.130
What's your name?

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:12.130
Harry Dennis.

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:13.200
Harry Dennis.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:14.620
Address?

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:16.620
2254 West 6th Avenue.

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:18.820
West 6th Avenue.

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:27.220
Nine o'clock Tuesday.

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:28.220
That's a cop for you.

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:30.000
Hands me a ticket while a baby murderer runs around.

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:31.980
- Why don't they do something about him?

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:47.270
- As long as you didn't hurt yourself.

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:50.430
What's the matter?

00:10:50.430 --> 00:10:52.470
- Oh. - Oh?

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:53.870
Well, come on.

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:54.690
I'm up here.

00:10:54.690 --> 00:10:56.720
Ah, sir.

00:11:22.460 --> 00:11:23.660
- There's a man up there with a kid.

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:27.630
- Oh, not again.

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:29.730
- Better get home and take care of that ankle.

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:59.970
live near here? Just around the corner. What's it to you, Mr. Where She Lives? Well, I was only trying to. The child, her foot. What about her foot? It looks hard to me. What is it all about? Who did what to her? I saw him first. He grabbed a kid and tried to take her shoes off. Did you say shoes? Tell them I didn't do anything. I didn't do anything. I swear I didn't do anything. I'll tell you, Mayor, we're doing everything possible. We may pick up that murderer in the next

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.660
five minutes or we may never find him.

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:03.450
All we can do is follow every lead.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:05.470
You're not dealing with a punk or a tin horn.

00:12:05.470 --> 00:12:07.660
Usual procedure won't work.

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:11.640
Catching this man is gonna take brains, imagination.

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:13.400
- Maybe you have some ideas we can use.

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:15.120
- Ideas, I got a million of them.

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:17.280
It's not my job to run this department, it's yours.

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:20.490
I got a city to run, this is only one department.

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:22.750
People in the city depend on me for transportation,

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:25.290
for hospitals, for sanitation.

00:12:25.290 --> 00:12:30.000
Not to go out and catch this murderer.

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:32.420
- Send him in.

00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:41.200
Carney, he can bring you up to date.

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:43.160
- I'm sorry, Mr. Mayor, I haven't got him yet.

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:44.120
- Course you haven't.

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:45.390
You know why?

00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:46.650
You're not thinking it through.

00:12:46.650 --> 00:12:48.940
Now listen, take a tip, use this.

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:50.260
Put yourself in Keller's place.

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:53.040
What would you do if you were Keller?

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:55.640
Figure that out and you've got your man.

00:12:55.640 --> 00:12:57.200
- Could be, Your Honor.

00:12:57.200 --> 00:13:00.000
- Brains, imagination, just like

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:03.620
Meanwhile, though, it's all right if I continue the raids all over town.

00:13:03.620 --> 00:13:05.620
Sure, sure, can't do any harm.

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:08.800
Put a scare into the punks and the tin horns.

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:09.820
Good for them.

00:13:09.820 --> 00:13:11.060
Well, I got to leave now.

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:12.060
I'm ten minutes behind schedule.

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:14.110
Got to open a big supermarket.

00:13:14.110 --> 00:13:16.950
Now, remember, brains, huh?

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:17.930
Imagination.

00:13:17.930 --> 00:13:19.360
Spencer, get the escort.

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:20.360
I'll be right down.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:25.500
You got him?

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:26.520
Yeah.

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:30.000
Can't blame him.

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:33.060
So the papers are really on our necks.

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:37.300
The ordinary murder, you look for a dame or a bank book.

00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:39.090
Got a victim with known enemies.

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:41.160
What do we got?

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:43.840
The missing shoes.

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:46.640
What are we looking for?

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:50.260
A man with a twisted mind.

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:51.750
Could be anybody.

00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:55.430
- Come on, come on, come on.

00:13:55.430 --> 00:14:00.000
- Oh, look, maybe he's the one, the things, get him!

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:01.030
What's going on?

00:14:01.030 --> 00:14:02.030
None of your business.

00:14:02.030 --> 00:14:03.030
Not so fast, buddy.

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:05.030
Here, take your hand off me.

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:06.020
Daddy!

00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:06.920
Daddy!

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:10.190
Daddy!

00:14:10.190 --> 00:14:13.100
That's all right, buddy.

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:13.930
All right, let's go.

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:21.130
I thought he was the kidnapper.

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:22.120
But shut up.

00:14:31.690 --> 00:14:36.080
- I don't know. I... I don't know how to... - Homicide, Finley.

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:39.460
- I can't bring him. - Now, see this kid comes walking by the screen?

00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:43.420
- Yeah, she's wearing a blue dress. - You got that wrong, she was wearing a red dress.

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:46.760
- Look, lady, I ain't colorblind. So this kid a blue dress comes along.

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:49.760
- It was a red dress. - What are you, a communist?

00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:54.830
- And as soon as I get in this guy's car, I see a little pair of shoes hanging from the dashboard.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:58.710
So I get out and run, but not before I had a chance to get his license number.

00:14:58.710 --> 00:14:59.890
- Thanks, sister.

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:03.740
You got to remember, the 10,000 of those gilded shoes hanging in cars in this town.

00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:05.900
There was something about this guy.

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:07.580
Oh, look in his eyes.

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:09.460
Fresh.

00:15:09.990 --> 00:15:11.470
Come on inside.

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:15.030
I just washed out the last bum we picked up.

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:16.930
And we ought to widen the field.

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:19.480
Bums don't suit for false arrest.

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:25.130
We keep on picking out bums, and the guy we're looking for could be a professor, a storekeeper.

00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:26.960
Maybe even a cop.

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:30.000
We look for him in hunky-tongs.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.580
and that he could be on a golf course.

00:15:32.580 --> 00:15:34.850
There's a new batch to check on him.

00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:37.830
The asylums are finally sending in lists of men

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:38.830
they've released who might be involved

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:40.430
in this kind of killing.

00:15:40.430 --> 00:15:43.260
Laws, files, reports.

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:46.600
I'll trade them all for one good stool pigeon.

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:51.490
Maybe you'll find your stool pigeon at the night's shakeout.

00:15:51.490 --> 00:15:52.490
Yup, Carney speaking.

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:56.000
Huh?

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:58.320
Where?

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:03.530
- Shoes again, huh?

00:16:03.530 --> 00:16:06.630
- 131 to Peter Walker and 131 to Peter Walker.

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:10.650
- Another one was six.

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:13.390
- I can't believe it.

00:16:13.390 --> 00:16:20.460
I can't believe it, that my baby.

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:22.440
- We read about those other children in the papers,

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:26.430
but our baby.

00:16:26.430 --> 00:16:29.070
- It could be anyone's child, anyone's.

00:16:29.070 --> 00:16:29.890
Nobody's safe.

00:16:31.370 --> 00:16:42.710
Such a beautiful baby, her hair was so long, like silk, when you touched it.

00:16:42.710 --> 00:16:45.550
If we need you, we'll get in touch with you.

00:16:45.550 --> 00:16:47.030
Thank you.

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:05.600
Maybe it's a mistake, maybe it's somebody else's.

00:17:32.140 --> 00:17:33.940
- No, we're really in for it.

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:36.440
A councilman's grandchild.

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:38.820
I tell you, we've got to find that killer.

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:40.330
- Maybe tonight, Chief.

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:41.710
Maybe one of the raids.

00:17:41.710 --> 00:17:42.550
- Do you really think

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:52.900
of this program but our time is up be with us again tomorrow evening for an

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:56.330
hour of classical music and now for a message

00:20:04.090 --> 00:20:30.000
The thrill of my life

00:20:33.610 --> 00:20:41.430
A matinee that played wasn't long, so we stayed a sort of second matinee.

00:20:41.430 --> 00:20:47.060
Good editor Henry does a thing right, his matinee does no doubt.

00:21:15.800 --> 00:21:17.990
- Shut 'em up. - Take it easy.

00:21:35.880 --> 00:21:38.940
You want us to find the baby killer, huh?

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:40.360
Well, this shakedown is to find him.

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:48.560
We figured it might be one of you.

00:21:48.560 --> 00:21:52.960
Anybody lose anything?

00:21:52.960 --> 00:21:55.900
I'm going to ask some questions, and I want some straight answers.

00:21:55.900 --> 00:21:56.740
I'll take you one at a time.

00:21:56.740 --> 00:21:58.940
You first.

00:21:58.940 --> 00:21:59.830
Mary Larkin.

00:22:00.600 --> 00:22:01.640
- Please, my mother.

00:22:01.640 --> 00:22:04.230
- They're all orphans 'til you pick 'em up.

00:22:04.230 --> 00:22:07.450
I'll bet she's got an arrest record as long as my arm.

00:22:07.450 --> 00:22:08.270
- Is he right?

00:22:08.270 --> 00:22:11.300
- No, honest, it's the first time I ever...

00:22:11.300 --> 00:22:12.620
Please let me go.

00:22:12.620 --> 00:22:15.090
- Get out of here and don't let me see you again.

00:22:15.090 --> 00:22:16.820
- Five will get you six, you will.

00:22:16.820 --> 00:22:18.930
- Next, name?

00:22:18.930 --> 00:22:20.270
- Greer, Harry Greer.

00:22:20.270 --> 00:22:22.230
I'm a salesman, I just happen to be in the neighborhood.

00:22:22.230 --> 00:22:23.550
- Yeah, how's business?

00:22:23.550 --> 00:22:26.170
- Could be better, things are bad all over.

00:22:26.170 --> 00:22:30.000
- I haven't seen a paper all day.

00:22:30.060 --> 00:22:34.210
Blue top, 5th temperance, 5th to win, Raja 6th at church.

00:22:34.210 --> 00:22:35.320
Better stick around, Greer,

00:22:35.320 --> 00:22:37.320
until we get the later edition of the final result.

00:22:37.320 --> 00:22:43.720
What are you doing down here?

00:22:43.720 --> 00:22:44.740
Shlummin'.

00:22:49.300 --> 00:22:54.040
Next.

00:23:02.400 --> 00:23:03.400
Gee, that guy, isn't it?

00:23:03.400 --> 00:23:04.700
Langley, Don Langley.

00:23:04.700 --> 00:23:06.340
Good lawyer, used to be.

00:23:06.340 --> 00:23:09.350
Who's next?

00:23:09.350 --> 00:23:13.030
Name?

00:23:13.030 --> 00:23:14.210
Mabel Smith.

00:23:14.210 --> 00:23:27.640
Boys, I asked you here to catch you up to date on my thinking about these baby killings.

00:23:27.640 --> 00:23:29.700
Very smart.

00:23:31.630 --> 00:23:33.430
I'm a very smart man, boss.

00:23:33.430 --> 00:23:35.870
I had this figured.

00:23:35.870 --> 00:23:37.170
Thanks.

00:23:37.170 --> 00:23:40.050
I always welcome your opinion, Rigott.

00:23:40.050 --> 00:23:43.120
But just why did you think I'm smart?

00:23:43.120 --> 00:23:45.570
And what was it you had figured?

00:23:45.570 --> 00:23:50.420
Well, you rigged the killings, didn't you, boss?

00:23:50.420 --> 00:23:54.260
To take the heat off us from the grand jury?

00:23:54.260 --> 00:23:55.940
Didn't you, boss?

00:23:55.940 --> 00:23:58.560
I thought it was a good idea.

00:23:58.560 --> 00:24:00.000
The heat's off.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:03.260
We're off the front pages, ain't we?

00:24:03.260 --> 00:24:07.800
The grand jury's investigating the cops instead of us.

00:24:07.800 --> 00:24:10.070
Ain't they, huh?

00:24:10.070 --> 00:24:12.080
Ain't they?

00:24:12.080 --> 00:24:18.410
You know, I'm glad I'm smarter than you think I am, Riggett.

00:24:18.410 --> 00:24:26.550
Sorry I'm late, Charlie.

00:24:26.550 --> 00:24:29.710
I...

00:24:30.160 --> 00:24:32.580
Stuffed in at Nick's for a drink.

00:24:32.580 --> 00:24:35.680
The place was veritably crawling with coppers.

00:24:35.680 --> 00:24:37.050
- I'll take that.

00:24:37.050 --> 00:24:38.910
- Thank you, Charlie.

00:24:38.910 --> 00:24:40.580
I need a shot.

00:24:40.580 --> 00:24:45.530
- I'm glad you're here to defend me, Dan.

00:24:45.530 --> 00:24:48.310
Rigger just said that I'm the baby killer.

00:24:48.310 --> 00:24:50.810
- Oh, I didn't mean you personally, boss.

00:24:50.810 --> 00:24:53.340
- Make me a case, counselor.

00:24:53.340 --> 00:24:57.750
I'll need that glass.

00:24:57.750 --> 00:24:58.840
Make me a case.

00:25:08.730 --> 00:25:13.250
- Gentlemen of the jury, I'll be brief.

00:25:13.250 --> 00:25:14.970
I know we're all anxious to get away.

00:25:14.970 --> 00:25:18.790
I myself have a very important case waiting.

00:25:18.790 --> 00:25:23.590
Case of scotch.

00:25:23.590 --> 00:25:27.140
But believe me gentlemen, this is the most important case

00:25:27.140 --> 00:25:28.900
since I went to the bar.

00:25:31.790 --> 00:25:34.310
Mr. Marshall here is not only my client, he's my friend.

00:25:34.310 --> 00:25:36.810
I've known him for years, since he was a boy.

00:25:36.810 --> 00:25:40.690
He was a good boy, good to his mother.

00:25:40.690 --> 00:25:43.520
Gentlemen, you have the faces of honest men,

00:25:43.520 --> 00:25:44.640
good judges of character.

00:25:44.640 --> 00:25:45.480
Look at my client.

00:25:45.480 --> 00:25:48.580
You judge for yourselves whether he would be capable

00:25:48.580 --> 00:25:52.530
of these heinous crimes by simply asking yourselves

00:25:52.530 --> 00:25:57.130
whether you, you for instance,

00:25:57.130 --> 00:25:59.920
would be capable of killing an innocent baby.

00:26:06.780 --> 00:26:08.600
- There's some things I don't like.

00:26:08.600 --> 00:26:11.360
- Exactly.

00:26:11.360 --> 00:26:12.350
See, Rigott?

00:26:12.350 --> 00:26:15.210
The thought of these murders turns even Patsy's stomach.

00:26:15.210 --> 00:26:18.090
Imagine the feelings of the general public.

00:26:18.090 --> 00:26:20.130
Your average citizen isn't too concerned

00:26:20.130 --> 00:26:22.580
whether the police catch us or not,

00:26:22.580 --> 00:26:25.810
lest the press stirs 'em up for political reasons,

00:26:25.810 --> 00:26:27.250
because in one way or another,

00:26:27.250 --> 00:26:29.440
we service almost the entire community.

00:26:30.540 --> 00:26:33.880
When it comes to catching a baby killer, they want action from their police department.

00:26:34.080 --> 00:26:36.000
That's what I say. They're on the spot.

00:26:36.080 --> 00:26:36.880
So what do they do?

00:26:37.880 --> 00:26:41.700
The counselor here has told us what happened at Knicks.

00:26:43.870 --> 00:26:45.350
How's your floating crap game, Sutro?

00:26:45.680 --> 00:26:46.490
Just floating.

00:26:48.090 --> 00:26:50.190
Keeping its head above water, but that's about all.

00:26:51.640 --> 00:26:53.800
A few of the boys got tabbed, so they've been laying low.

00:26:53.940 --> 00:26:54.680
That's what I thought.

00:26:56.770 --> 00:26:57.190
McMahon?

00:26:58.300 --> 00:26:58.970
Same.

00:26:59.450 --> 00:26:59.920
Or worse.

00:27:01.240 --> 00:27:04.770
- You know, you can't even show your face around a high school nowadays. - Batsy.

00:27:04.770 --> 00:27:09.040
Where's the cops get the idea that baby killers play slot machines?

00:27:09.040 --> 00:27:11.590
Sure, boss, it's the same with us.

00:27:11.590 --> 00:27:14.110
They've been tapping a lot of our little bookies.

00:27:14.110 --> 00:27:16.770
- Cigar store, barbershop stuff. - Reagan!

00:27:16.770 --> 00:27:19.720
Excuse me, Counselor.

00:27:19.720 --> 00:27:21.900
What do you think that means?

00:27:21.900 --> 00:27:27.010
People who live in glass houses shouldn't throw stones.

00:27:27.010 --> 00:27:29.000
I don't know, boss. I...

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:31.800
We're in a business with a tank of millions.

00:27:31.800 --> 00:27:35.020
From Patsy's slot machines to your wire service.

00:27:35.880 --> 00:27:39.960
These are the runners, the pickup men.

00:27:39.960 --> 00:27:41.670
They collect the first money.

00:27:41.670 --> 00:27:45.760
These are the drops, the district officers.

00:27:45.760 --> 00:27:48.310
This is the center, you boys.

00:27:48.310 --> 00:27:50.130
And this is me.

00:27:50.130 --> 00:27:52.090
We're on the top there.

00:27:52.090 --> 00:27:56.320
Rickert, you think everything is lovely

00:27:56.320 --> 00:27:58.130
just because we're not in front of the grand jury

00:27:58.130 --> 00:28:00.000
and your face isn't on the front pages.

00:28:00.350 --> 00:28:02.920
- Sure. - Yeah, sure.

00:28:02.920 --> 00:28:05.050
But now look what happens on the top there

00:28:05.050 --> 00:28:08.780
when the bugger was knocked out.

00:28:08.780 --> 00:28:15.810
Now do you understand?

00:28:15.810 --> 00:28:17.250
Clean up the mess, counselor.

00:28:17.250 --> 00:28:29.410
So what, boss?

00:28:31.530 --> 00:28:35.780
- The police department answers public pressure by raiding us.

00:28:35.780 --> 00:28:37.640
Raids, raids, and more raids.

00:28:37.640 --> 00:28:39.980
They're on the spot.

00:28:39.980 --> 00:28:42.190
Well, to protect ourselves,

00:28:42.190 --> 00:28:44.410
we've gotta take 'em off the spot.

00:28:44.410 --> 00:28:46.930
- Where do we get off helping the cops?

00:28:46.930 --> 00:28:48.290
Who ever heard of something like that?

00:28:48.290 --> 00:28:49.610
- I'll admit it's a situation

00:28:49.610 --> 00:28:51.650
we could never have anticipated.

00:28:51.650 --> 00:28:53.900
- Force majeure.

00:28:53.900 --> 00:28:56.270
- Force majeure.

00:28:56.270 --> 00:28:58.420
Thank you, counselor.

00:28:58.420 --> 00:28:59.960
An act of God, Sutro.

00:29:00.860 --> 00:29:03.140
But it can't go on.

00:29:03.140 --> 00:29:07.160
As long as this man is running loose, we can't operate.

00:29:07.160 --> 00:29:09.110
Who do we frame?

00:29:09.110 --> 00:29:11.810
No frame, Riggett.

00:29:11.810 --> 00:29:15.300
This killer isn't gonna stop just because they make an arrest.

00:29:15.300 --> 00:29:17.700
We have gotta find 'em and stop 'em ourselves.

00:29:17.700 --> 00:29:20.180
Oh, we ain't gonna help the cops, we're gonna be the cops.

00:29:20.180 --> 00:29:24.140
We've got the organization to keep an eye on every child in this city.

00:29:24.140 --> 00:29:27.810
Our runners and pickup men are on the streets all the time.

00:29:27.810 --> 00:29:29.920
We've got drops in candy stores.

00:29:30.090 --> 00:29:32.790
Barbershops, newsstands, shoeshine parlors.

00:29:33.270 --> 00:29:37.750
We've even got our own radio system, our cabs, the Ajax outfit.

00:29:38.260 --> 00:29:40.560
With that two-way system, they cover this town.

00:29:41.480 --> 00:29:45.480
Oh, yeah, I see it. My boys will be dishing out a third degree for a change.

00:29:46.680 --> 00:29:47.920
They're gonna like that.

00:29:48.040 --> 00:29:49.540
What an operation this is gonna be.

00:29:49.640 --> 00:29:54.680
That's right. A major operation. Operation M.

00:29:54.770 --> 00:29:56.610
M? I don't get it.

00:29:57.210 --> 00:29:59.440
M for murderer. Dope.

00:30:01.080 --> 00:30:02.570
All right, now, you know what to do.

00:30:02.570 --> 00:30:03.650
Here's one for you.

00:30:03.650 --> 00:30:05.410
For you.

00:30:05.410 --> 00:30:08.530
Hey, uh, keep your eyes open when you're out there on the street.

00:30:08.530 --> 00:30:10.550
Particularly when you're in the alleys.

00:30:19.120 --> 00:30:22.980
Ninety-three, Bob.

00:30:35.150 --> 00:30:54.700
...on each of you boys and your gangs to watch his own territory.

00:30:54.700 --> 00:30:57.220
No chiseling, no arguments.

00:30:57.220 --> 00:31:00.000
We'll start your fighting again in the afternoon.

00:31:00.120 --> 00:31:01.800
- Where you find this guy, get me?

00:31:01.800 --> 00:31:02.640
- Yeah, sure.

00:31:02.640 --> 00:31:03.400
- Okay, boss.

00:31:03.400 --> 00:31:04.240
- Right, boss.

00:31:04.240 --> 00:31:07.270
- Remember, the minute you make this guy call my number.

00:31:07.270 --> 00:31:10.050
Any Ajax driver will give you a hand.

00:31:10.050 --> 00:31:16.890
Meanwhile, we're gonna take care of expenses.

00:31:16.890 --> 00:31:17.670
- Thanks, boss.

00:32:04.190 --> 00:32:08.160
Ajax, 48 again, false alarm, everything's OK.

00:32:53.930 --> 00:32:56.770
Well, I picked up that bunch from Malaysian Hospital reporting.

00:32:56.770 --> 00:32:58.230
Turned Graham's office now.

00:32:58.230 --> 00:32:59.480
Good.

00:33:00.320 --> 00:33:02.880
He'll play games with 'em, rub their heads and turn 'em loose.

00:33:02.880 --> 00:33:05.860
What does he expect to get out of 'em that way?

00:33:05.860 --> 00:33:09.210
- You got a better way? - Yeah.

00:33:09.210 --> 00:33:13.590
A dark room and a rubber hose and about a half a dozen cops.

00:33:13.590 --> 00:33:16.250
- The courts don't like it that way. - Yeah, that's just the trouble.

00:33:16.250 --> 00:33:19.260
We need less courts and more cops.

00:33:19.260 --> 00:33:21.960
Well, I got some more loonies to look up.

00:33:21.960 --> 00:33:26.010
How come if they're psychos, the hospital turns 'em loose in the first place?

00:33:26.010 --> 00:33:28.920
- It's the law, they're cured. - No, they're cured.

00:33:28.920 --> 00:33:30.000
A fat chance of cops

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:32.220
I've got to make a pinch stick.

00:33:32.220 --> 00:33:43.380
Laws, cords, skull tappers.

00:33:43.380 --> 00:33:50.590
- Head, green, red.

00:33:50.590 --> 00:33:54.150
- Sing, song.

00:33:54.150 --> 00:33:55.550
- Shoes.

00:33:55.550 --> 00:33:58.270
- Stockings.

00:33:58.270 --> 00:33:58.870
- Water.

00:34:01.400 --> 00:34:03.620
- Land?

00:34:03.620 --> 00:34:04.550
- String?

00:34:04.550 --> 00:34:08.050
- Choke.

00:34:08.050 --> 00:34:10.190
- Tell me what you see, or what it could be,

00:34:10.190 --> 00:34:15.750
or what you imagine it to be.

00:34:15.750 --> 00:34:22.930
- I see two teddy bears, a Christmas tree in the corner,

00:34:22.930 --> 00:34:27.110
a man with a bandage on his head.

00:34:27.110 --> 00:34:29.730
- And flames rising in the air,

00:34:30.540 --> 00:34:39.890
and a sword, and a horse with his hoofs in the air.

00:34:44.020 --> 00:34:55.900
- All right, thank you.

00:34:55.900 --> 00:34:57.740
- Any leads on that punch?

00:34:57.740 --> 00:35:00.000
- Just the one, the fellow that answered.

00:35:00.090 --> 00:35:02.490
choked a string, probably won't mean anything.

00:35:02.490 --> 00:35:03.490
- What are you looking for?

00:35:03.490 --> 00:35:04.980
What kind of a man?

00:35:04.980 --> 00:35:06.580
- Probably a schizophrenic,

00:35:06.580 --> 00:35:08.760
possibly a paranoid schizophrenic,

00:35:08.760 --> 00:35:10.570
maybe a borderline case.

00:35:10.570 --> 00:35:12.980
But in any event, a very sick man.

00:35:12.980 --> 00:35:14.620
Frequently, this form of mental disease

00:35:14.620 --> 00:35:16.840
can be traced back to the patient's childhood,

00:35:16.840 --> 00:35:19.610
to some severe emotional injury he suffered.

00:35:19.610 --> 00:35:21.990
- You mean what Carney's men call psychos?

00:35:21.990 --> 00:35:22.990
Ting-a-lings?

00:35:22.990 --> 00:35:26.680
- Well, in picturesque lay language, possibly yes.

00:35:26.680 --> 00:35:29.130
This man lives in a world all his own.

00:35:29.130 --> 00:35:30.000
Within that world,

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:33.680
his ability to think clearly need not necessarily be affected.

00:35:33.680 --> 00:35:35.020
- What about the missing shoes?

00:35:35.020 --> 00:35:36.220
What does that mean?

00:35:36.220 --> 00:35:39.510
- Well, for Carney, they provide a clue to find the man.

00:35:39.510 --> 00:35:41.650
But I have to find the man before I can get a clue

00:35:41.650 --> 00:35:43.200
to the missing shoes.

00:35:43.200 --> 00:35:45.900
Then that too may have resulted from some childhood injury

00:35:45.900 --> 00:35:47.500
or serious neglect.

00:35:47.500 --> 00:35:50.000
Something happened then that made shoes a detonator

00:35:50.000 --> 00:35:53.430
that sets him off.

00:35:53.430 --> 00:35:54.290
- All right, come on.

00:35:54.290 --> 00:35:55.790
Thanks, Doc.

00:35:55.790 --> 00:35:56.600
- So long, Doc.

00:36:22.200 --> 00:36:24.450
$8 a week in advance.

00:36:24.450 --> 00:36:28.970
In the health department, does a man named Harrell live here?

00:36:28.970 --> 00:36:29.920
Well, what's he done?

00:36:30.960 --> 00:36:32.520
He spent some time in a hospital.

00:36:32.520 --> 00:36:33.460
Oh, yeah, that's right.

00:36:33.460 --> 00:36:35.120
He does talk about his headaches a lot.

00:36:35.120 --> 00:36:36.680
Well, that's what I want to talk to him about.

00:36:36.680 --> 00:36:38.200
I thought maybe he'd like to back to the hospital

00:36:38.200 --> 00:36:39.060
for some more treatment.

00:36:39.060 --> 00:36:40.840
Oh, Mr. Harrow ain't in.

00:36:40.840 --> 00:36:43.460
You mind if I wait for him?

00:36:43.460 --> 00:36:45.190
I guess it's all right.

00:36:45.190 --> 00:36:47.230
Oh, that's my dinner boiling over.

00:36:47.230 --> 00:36:49.270
Just down the hall, second door to the left.

00:40:24.060 --> 00:40:27.620
Hello honey, you should wait for me at home.

00:40:59.660 --> 00:41:00.000
of it.

00:42:01.120 --> 00:42:07.110
- Waiter. Waiter. Whiskey. - Mervin or rye?

00:42:07.520 --> 00:42:08.870
- I don't. Any kind.

00:42:36.140 --> 00:42:39.070
- Died in the state hospital seven months ago.

00:42:39.070 --> 00:42:41.270
Harrell wasn't in, conducted a search of his room,

00:42:41.270 --> 00:42:42.870
nothing suspicious.

00:42:42.870 --> 00:42:47.190
Just the same, I may have he picked up later on anyway.

00:42:47.190 --> 00:42:49.820
Hobbs, living with his parents has a perfect alibi.

00:42:49.820 --> 00:42:51.950
- Okay, okay, that's enough.

00:42:51.950 --> 00:42:53.620
Dead ones, missing ones.

00:42:53.620 --> 00:42:55.810
Men with perfect alibis.

00:42:55.810 --> 00:42:57.680
Maybe nobody committed these murders.

00:43:00.700 --> 00:43:06.370
-Everything's gotta happen to me. -Hey, maybe I'm nuts.

00:43:09.740 --> 00:43:28.740
-Maybe. -Maybe.

00:43:30.220 --> 00:43:38.890
Let's get to work.

00:43:38.890 --> 00:43:42.020
Nothing, nothing at all, just the same.

00:43:42.020 --> 00:43:43.670
Just the same, there's something.

00:45:11.840 --> 00:45:13.300
- Shut up, what's the beef?

00:45:13.300 --> 00:45:14.380
- You hear that?

00:45:14.380 --> 00:45:15.660
You hear that music?

00:45:15.660 --> 00:45:17.560
- Yeah, some tin whistle, so what?

00:45:17.560 --> 00:45:18.660
Some guy and a little kid.

00:45:18.660 --> 00:45:20.600
- It's him, it's him, the murderer.

00:45:20.600 --> 00:45:21.900
I heard that song before.

00:45:21.900 --> 00:45:23.040
He's the man that bought the balloon

00:45:23.040 --> 00:45:24.740
the day that Elsie Costa was murdered.

00:46:07.100 --> 00:46:08.160
I'll show you a trick.

00:46:50.920 --> 00:46:53.250
Have a match?

00:46:53.250 --> 00:46:54.250
Have a match?

00:46:54.250 --> 00:46:55.250
How about giving your old buddy a beer, girl?

00:46:55.250 --> 00:46:56.250
No.

00:46:56.250 --> 00:46:57.250
Just buy me a little drink, that's all.

00:46:57.250 --> 00:46:58.250
No.

00:46:58.250 --> 00:47:00.000
What's the matter if you don't drink, no drink?

00:47:00.190 --> 00:47:01.720
Bearing nothing.

00:47:01.720 --> 00:47:03.590
Dry you off.

00:47:03.590 --> 00:47:15.870
No, never mind.

00:47:15.870 --> 00:47:18.890
Yeah!

00:47:18.890 --> 00:47:25.090
You want some flowers?

00:47:25.090 --> 00:47:25.800
Yeah.

00:47:31.630 --> 00:47:33.390
- Can you have some ice cream?

00:47:33.390 --> 00:47:34.820
- What kind do you want?

00:47:34.820 --> 00:47:36.010
- Strawberry.

00:47:36.010 --> 00:47:42.130
Hey, mister, you got something on your back.

00:47:42.130 --> 00:47:57.070
I'll brush it off for you.

00:47:57.070 --> 00:47:59.120
- They're chasing us, we gotta hurry.

00:48:15.770 --> 00:48:17.270
What's cooking? Who are you tailing?

00:48:17.270 --> 00:48:18.850
It's my sidekick here.

00:48:18.850 --> 00:48:21.350
His chick's two-timing, and we're just doing a little checking.

00:48:21.350 --> 00:48:23.300
Yeah, well, I think I'll do some checking myself.

00:48:23.300 --> 00:48:25.500
Say, you. Come here.

00:48:25.500 --> 00:48:28.230
Charlie, they found him. They spotted him.

00:48:33.680 --> 00:48:38.190
Stay with him. There's a C-note for you, if he's the right man.

00:48:38.190 --> 00:48:44.020
I knew they'd find him.

00:48:44.020 --> 00:48:46.780
The kid even branded him. Plastered an M on his back.

00:48:46.780 --> 00:48:47.920
Suppose he gets away?

00:48:47.920 --> 00:48:52.680
He won't. That's the value of organization and knowing how to run it.

00:48:52.680 --> 00:48:54.280
Call Ajax.

00:48:54.280 --> 00:48:58.230
Have the dispatcher notify the drivers to pass the word around, quick.

00:48:58.230 --> 00:48:59.730
It's in the bag.

00:49:00.190 --> 00:49:02.190
Doesn't this call for a celebration?

00:49:02.190 --> 00:49:04.380
Don't mind us, Counselor.

00:49:04.380 --> 00:49:09.370
Drink yours straight from the bottle.

00:49:09.370 --> 00:49:12.910
Becker's staked out in Harrow's room as a general alarm out.

00:49:12.910 --> 00:49:14.910
Plainclothesmen are blanketing the district.

00:49:14.910 --> 00:49:18.600
The uniformed division's making every downtown saloon.

00:49:18.600 --> 00:49:20.550
We'll pick him up, don't worry.

00:49:20.550 --> 00:49:23.110
We better. The mayor's on his way down here.

00:49:23.110 --> 00:49:28.770
His statement ought to make the morning papers.

00:49:28.770 --> 00:49:29.780
We'll pick him up, but then what?

00:49:30.090 --> 00:49:32.690
Back to the booby hatch?

00:49:32.690 --> 00:49:35.910
Man like Haro should never have been released in the first place.

00:49:35.910 --> 00:49:37.650
Hospital's so understaffed.

00:49:37.650 --> 00:49:39.750
They free dangerous men.

00:49:39.750 --> 00:49:41.660
But they won't get out this time.

00:49:41.660 --> 00:49:45.390
He'll burn.

00:49:45.390 --> 00:49:46.760
That's right.

00:49:46.760 --> 00:49:51.490
That's right.

00:49:51.490 --> 00:49:55.730
That'll fix everything.

00:50:20.350 --> 00:50:21.730
We're still playing our game.

00:50:21.730 --> 00:50:23.240
- I'm tired. - No, no.

00:51:30.320 --> 00:51:33.660
- Sees everything here, everything, don't kid me.

00:51:33.660 --> 00:51:35.160
Well, have a good time, see you Monday.

00:51:35.160 --> 00:51:36.160
- Have a good time fishing, Pop.

00:51:36.160 --> 00:51:37.160
- Thank you.

00:51:40.050 --> 00:51:42.330
- Oh, come on out, come on, I ain't done all day,

00:51:42.330 --> 00:51:43.370
I gotta be going.

00:51:43.370 --> 00:51:45.630
- Hey, Pop, Pop, did you see a guy run through here?

00:51:45.630 --> 00:51:48.170
- Nah, nah, feed it, kids, no one came in here.

00:51:48.170 --> 00:51:50.450
- Hey, Pop, look!

00:51:50.450 --> 00:51:53.180
- All right now, boys, get, get.

00:51:53.180 --> 00:51:55.560
- No kidding, Pop, he's a dangerous character.

00:51:55.560 --> 00:51:57.830
- Yeah, I know, it's the baby killer.

00:51:57.830 --> 00:52:00.000
- Yeah, yeah, you're so smart.

00:52:00.350 --> 00:52:01.870
Well, that's who it is.

00:52:01.870 --> 00:52:04.580
Peter, Peter.

00:52:04.580 --> 00:52:05.580
You stay here.

00:52:05.580 --> 00:52:07.100
You guys go get Doug and the boys.

00:52:07.100 --> 00:52:08.100
OK, come on.

00:53:09.560 --> 00:53:10.960
in the building on 3rd Street.

00:53:10.960 --> 00:53:12.720
- Keep the place covered.

00:53:12.720 --> 00:53:15.700
Somebody will be around in a few minutes to give you a hand.

00:53:15.700 --> 00:53:16.940
That's all.

00:53:16.940 --> 00:53:18.550
- What a break.

00:53:18.550 --> 00:53:20.480
He's inside, we're out.

00:53:20.480 --> 00:53:22.290
What do we do now, call the cops?

00:53:22.290 --> 00:53:23.570
- We're going after 'em.

00:53:23.570 --> 00:53:24.950
- Yeah, sure.

00:53:24.950 --> 00:53:26.770
And tomorrow we crack Fort Knox.

00:53:26.770 --> 00:53:28.280
- Maybe Sutro's right, boss.

00:53:28.280 --> 00:53:30.000
Maybe we ought to tip off the cops.

00:53:30.030 --> 00:53:32.790
- He said we're going after him.

00:53:32.790 --> 00:53:34.440
- Mac. - Yeah?

00:53:34.440 --> 00:53:36.480
- Get down to Third Street.

00:53:36.480 --> 00:53:38.690
Call me when you know the score.

00:53:38.690 --> 00:53:39.560
Patsy?

00:53:39.560 --> 00:53:40.170
- Yeah?

00:53:40.170 --> 00:53:41.250
- Line up your muscle men,

00:53:41.250 --> 00:53:43.480
some boys who can crack a crib.

00:53:43.480 --> 00:53:46.690
Let 'em bring their kits.

00:53:46.690 --> 00:53:47.730
- Well, what are you waiting for?

00:53:47.730 --> 00:53:48.530
Get going!

00:54:10.520 --> 00:54:14.130
Hey, anybody inside?

00:54:14.130 --> 00:54:16.230
I'm locking up.

00:55:48.750 --> 00:55:50.510
Did you know your gate's unlocked?

00:55:50.510 --> 00:55:53.400
Huh? Why, why should I?

00:55:53.400 --> 00:55:56.490
Maybe those kids...

00:55:56.490 --> 00:55:58.290
Open up.

00:55:58.290 --> 00:55:58.960
Quick!

00:56:48.780 --> 00:56:52.040
All you gotta do is answer a couple of questions.

00:56:52.040 --> 00:56:55.210
How many watchmen in the building?

00:57:04.190 --> 00:57:07.190
How many?

00:57:07.190 --> 00:57:17.770
I'm the engineer.

00:57:17.770 --> 00:57:19.460
I'm Washington.

00:57:19.460 --> 00:57:20.640
I'm the engineer.

00:57:20.640 --> 00:57:21.770
The only ones in the building.

00:57:21.770 --> 00:57:24.960
OK, boy.

00:57:24.960 --> 00:57:27.260
Start with the cellar and end with the roof.

00:57:30.120 --> 00:57:32.760
Take a couple of boys and pick up the engineer.

00:57:32.760 --> 00:57:36.150
-Supro! -Men!

00:58:12.890 --> 00:58:15.810
Take him upstairs.

00:58:30.250 --> 00:58:31.440
- -

00:59:17.080 --> 00:59:19.240
- Any chance he got scared off?

00:59:19.240 --> 00:59:20.740
- No, nobody could tip him.

00:59:20.740 --> 00:59:23.400
I got the phones tapped and the joints closed up tight.

00:59:37.580 --> 00:59:39.640
- I haven't found him yet.

00:59:39.640 --> 00:59:42.130
- Who's talking?

00:59:42.130 --> 00:59:45.480
- Tell McMahon that Marshall will be right there.

00:59:45.480 --> 00:59:50.180
Stay here and watch the phone, and for once, stay sober.

00:59:50.180 --> 00:59:52.150
- To do a thing right is to do it yourself.

01:00:46.250 --> 01:00:47.210
about the alarm boxes.

01:00:47.210 --> 01:00:54.080
They have to be punched every hour.

01:00:54.080 --> 01:00:55.480
Take care of the alarm boxes.

01:00:55.480 --> 01:00:57.570
